[0.000, "o", "un its workflow                  \u001b(B\u001b[m       \u001b[92m\r\n      6 +\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m    npm run order -- ITEM [--quantity N]   # place an order and run its workflow\u001b[39m\u001b[11X\u001b[24;100H\u001b[1K\u001b[97m\r\n⏺\u001b[39m Now I'll place the order. The VM is still finishing setup, so this command will wait for it.      \u001b[27;1H  \u001b[37m\u001b[2mRan \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m\u001b[1m4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37m\u001b[2m shell commands \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[77X\u001b[97m\u001b[29;1H⏺\u001b[39m I added \u001b[94m--quantity\u001b[39m to \u001b[94morder.js\u001b[39m and placed the order for 2 espresso machines. The workflow         \r\n  completed, but the table does not show the quantity, because the schema has no column for it.     \u001b[31;100H\u001b[1K\r\n  Order line from the run:\u001b[74X\u001b[34;1H  \u001b[94morder #1: espresso machine x2\u001b[39m\u001b[69X\r\n    \u001b[94mreserved\u001b[39m\u001b[88X\r\n    \u001b[94mpayment timed out, retrying\u001b[39m\u001b[69X\r\n    \u001b[94mpaid\u001b[39m\u001b[92X\r\n    \u001b[94mshipped\u001b[39m\u001b[89X\r\n  \u001b[94mworkflow order-1 completed\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\u001b[40;100H\u001b[1K\r\n  Orders table:\u001b[85X\u001b[43;1H   \u001b[94mid |       item       | status  |\u001b[10X\u001b[10Ccreated_at\u001b[39m\u001b[44X\r\n  \u001b[94m----+------------"]
